<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Auth's cross-section surface, carved into its own leaf project because almost every
    consumer is in Base: IRoleAssignmentService alone is injected by ~30 production files —
    Humans.Application services (Users, Profiles, Shifts, GoogleIntegration), Humans.Infrastructure
    jobs and the metrics service, Shell's claims transformation and admin controllers, and twelve
    already-moved sections. A Contracts/ *folder* inside Humans.Auth would therefore make Base
    reference a section and cycle (design §15.5b,
    memory/architecture/section-project-cycle-fix.md).

    Framework-free by construction (Microsoft.NET.Sdk; no FrameworkReference): the one
    piece of Auth's public surface that needs ASP.NET — RoleAssignmentOperationRequirement,
    an IAuthorizationRequirement Shell's UsersAdminController passes to
    IAuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync — sits in Humans.Auth's own Contracts/ *folder*
    instead. Tickets was the first section to ship both halves; the split is what each may
    name (template step 5b).

    AssignRoleAsync/EndRoleAsync return the section's own RoleAssignmentResult rather than
    Humans.Onboarding.Contracts.OnboardingResult, which they returned in Base.

    Humans.Users.Contracts is the one leaf-to-leaf reference here, added with IMagicLinkService
    at nobodies-collective/Humans#866 G5 lane 4b-2i. It is forced, not chosen: two of that
    interface's members return Humans.Users.Contracts.User, and its Base consumer
    (Humans.Application's ExternalLoginService, which calls FindUserByVerifiedEmailAsync) cannot
    reference the Humans.Auth *section* project — design §15 step 5b's "a consumer in Base forces
    Humans.<Section>.Contracts", the same shape that put IUserService on the Users leaf. It is
    the third instance of the leaf-to-leaf edge the 2026-08-14 Base-floor decision lists for
    unwinding (Email.Contracts → Events.Contracts, Teams.Contracts → Auth.Contracts); it unwinds
    when User stops being the return type, not before.
  -->

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Humans.Interfaces\Humans.Interfaces.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Humans.Users.Contracts\Humans.Users.Contracts.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="NodaTime" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
